# What stays out of the image built by deploy/Dockerfile (`COPY . .`).
#
# Without this file the whole checkout was copied, so the production .env and
# its two .env.bak.* copies sat inside every image at /app/.env*: every secret
# readable by anyone who got a shell in a container or a copy of the image.
# The containers never read those files: compose passes the variables with
# `env_file: ../.env`, and settings.py reads only os.environ.

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
firebase-credentials.json
*.pem
*.key
*.jks

# Runtime data: mounted as volumes or created at start, never baked in
media/
staticfiles/
logs/
celerybeat-schedule*

# Repository and tooling
.git/
.gitignore
.claude/
.gstack/
.idea/
.vscode/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
